  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 9,
    "summary": "Rebuke a wise man and he will love you—The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom—The guests of an immoral woman are in the depths of hell.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Wisdom hath builded her house, she hath hewn out her seven pillars:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Alma 26:35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine; she hath also furnished her table.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "She hath sent forth her maidens: she crieth upon the highest places of the city,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: as for him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "D&C 1:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Come, eat of my bread, and drink of the wine which I have mingled.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Wisdom prepares her feast and invites participants."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Forsake the foolish, and live; and go in the way of understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "D&C 66:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Prov. 6:32."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that reproveth a scorner getteth to himself shame: and he that rebuketh a wicked man getteth himself a blot.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate thee: rebuke a wise man, and he will love thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Ps. 141:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Give instruction to a wise man, and he will be yet wiser: teach a just man, and he will increase in learning.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Teaching."
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "Matt. 13:12 (11–12); D&C 88:118."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "TG Learn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Prov. 30:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Holiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For by me thy days shall be multiplied, and the years of thy life shall be increased.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:55; Mosiah 14:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou be wise, thou shalt be wise for thyself: but if thou scornest, thou alone shalt bear it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Job 35:7 (6–8)."
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "Gal. 6:5 (4–5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A foolish woman is clamorous: she is simple, and knoweth nothing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Woman."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For she sitteth at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To call passengers who go right on their ways:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: and as for him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Stolen waters are sweet, and bread eaten in secret is pleasant.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But he knoweth not that the dead are there; and that her guests are in the depths of hell.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "Alma 12:11; D&C 29:38; 76:84 (84–86)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
